{"book":"integers","bookTitle":"Integers","concept":7,"title":"Order of operations with integers","grades":"Grade 8","goal":"I can calculate with integers in the correct order.","teach":"Work in this order: <b>brackets</b>, then <b>powers</b>, then <b>× and ÷</b> from left to right, then <b>+ and −</b> from left to right. Keep negative numbers in brackets so that you see their signs.","tvis":"<div class=\"vis\"><span class=\"vi\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" style=\"width:611px;height:auto\" viewBox=\"0 0 470 46\"><rect x=\"2.0\" y=\"2.0\" width=\"112.0\" height=\"42.0\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#555555\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"58.0\" y=\"28.0\" font-family=\"Public Sans\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#444444\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"normal\">1  Brackets</text><rect x=\"120.0\" y=\"2.0\" width=\"112.0\" height=\"42.0\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#555555\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"176.0\" y=\"28.0\" font-family=\"Public Sans\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#444444\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"normal\">2  Powers</text><rect x=\"238.0\" y=\"2.0\" width=\"112.0\" height=\"42.0\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#555555\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"294.0\" y=\"28.0\" font-family=\"Public Sans\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#444444\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"normal\">3  × and ÷</text><rect x=\"356.0\" y=\"2.0\" width=\"112.0\" height=\"42.0\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#555555\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"412.0\" y=\"28.0\" font-family=\"Public Sans\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#444444\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"normal\">4  + and −</text></svg></span></div>","ex":{"q":"Calculate −3 × 4 + 20 ÷ (−5).","steps":["Multiply and divide first: −3 × 4 = −12 and 20 ÷ (−5) = −4.","Now add: −12 + (−4).","The answer is −16."]},"watch":"−3² means −(3 × 3) = −9. (−3)² means (−3) × (−3) = 9.","qs":[{"text":"Calculate (−8 + 3) × (−2).","vis":"","parts":[{"t":"box","label":"Answer","a":"10","form":"val","o":null}],"hint":"Brackets first.","steps":"1. Rule (order of operations): brackets first, then powers, then × and ÷, then + and −.<br>2. Brackets: −8 + 3 = −5<br>3. (−5) × (−2) = 10"},{"text":"Calculate −12 ÷ 3 − 5.","vis":"","parts":[{"t":"box","label":"Answer","a":"-9","form":"val","o":null}],"hint":"Divide first.","steps":"1. Rule (order of operations): brackets first, then powers, then × and ÷, then + and −.<br>2. −12 ÷ 3 = −4<br>3. −4 − 5 = −9"},{"text":"Calculate 4 − 3 × (−6).","vis":"","parts":[{"t":"box","label":"Answer","a":"22","form":"val","o":null}],"hint":"3 × (−6) first.","steps":"1. Rule (order of operations): brackets first, then powers, then × and ÷, then + and −.<br>2. 3 × (−6) = −18<br>3. 4 − (−18) = 4 + 18 = 22"}]}